From 1a2c3d4e5f6071829384756abcdef0123456789 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LS1046A Canonical <canonical@ls1046a-build>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 21:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fman: fe_flow_add drop-ctx live trace (F-251)

The tc-flower hook (0198) inserts an EXIT-FE drop record via
fman_pcd_fe_flow_add(drop_action=1), but the board shows the delivered
record still ENQUEUEs instead of discarding (decomp/findings.md #42/43:
observed ctx=0x1, not the expected EXIT-singleton MURAM offset). The
debugfs 'add drop' verb (0197) exercises the *same* pcd->fe_exit_off
value directly and is silicon-proven to discard -- so this traces the
one code path (0196's rec_ctx ternary inside fman_pcd_fe_flow_add) that
has never been exercised by a live caller before 0198. One pr_info,
gated on drop_action, right where rec_ctx is computed: prints
pcd->fe_exit_off, enq_obj->muram_off, and the resulting rec_ctx at the
moment the flower path reaches this call, so a board dmesg capture
during a flower insert tells us directly whether fe_exit_off itself is
sane here or whether the bug is downstream of this computation.

Patch-Name: 0199-fman-pcd-fe-flow-add-drop-ctx-trace.patch
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
index 02ba43bc9212..1b2c3d4e5f60 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/fman/fman_pcd.c
@@ -5113,6 +5113,15 @@ int fman_pcd_fe_flow_add(struct fman *fm, u8 hw_port_id,
 		 * are irrelevant. */
 		unsigned long rec_ctx = action->drop_action ?
 					pcd->fe_exit_off : (u32)enq_obj->muram_off;
+		/* F-251 (0199): live trace of the drop-ctx computation -- is
+		 * pcd->fe_exit_off actually the sane nonzero MURAM offset the
+		 * debugfs 'add drop' path (0197) observed, at the moment a
+		 * production caller (the tc-flower hook, 0198) reaches here? */
+		if (action->drop_action)
+			pr_info("fman_pcd: F-251 drop-ctx port=%u fe_exit_off=%#lx enq_muram=%#x rec_ctx=%#lx hit_fqid=%u key_size=%u tbl_idx=%u\n",
+				hw_port_id, pcd->fe_exit_off, enq_obj->muram_off,
+				rec_ctx, hit_fqid, action->key_size,
+				action->table_idx);
 		err = fman_pcd_ehash_add_key(t, action->key, action->key_size,
 						 (u32)rec_ctx, hit_fqid,
 						 false /* F-189(genl-stats-false) */,
--
2.43.0
